- Delegate to the A2A hub for long-running tasks via `delegate_task`

## Issue Creation Workflow

When creating a new feature/satellite/enhancement issue:

1. **Create the issue** (dispatch `github-ops` or do it directly):
   ```bash
   gh issue create --repo The-Replacement/hub --title "<title>" --body "<body>" --label "enhancement"
   ```
   Note the issue number returned.

2. **Add it to the board** immediately:
   ```bash
   gh project item-add {{ board_number }} --owner {{ board_owner }} --url "<ISSUE_URL>"
   ```

3. **Set initial board state** (the issue starts as Todo):
   ```bash
   n3rv board sync --issue <N> --phase todo
   ```

4. **Return the issue number** to the user. They can then run `/sdd-new --issue <N> <description>`.

## Project Board Integration

The **The-Replacement Roadmap** project board (org `{{ board_owner }}`, project #{{ board_number }}) tracks all work items. When running SDD phases, always include the issue number so subagents can auto-update the board.

`n3rv board sync --issue <N> --phase <PHASE>` is the only board writer: it resolves the item with complete pagination, asserts exactly one match, updates Status and SDD Phase together, and exits non-zero when the issue is not on the board. Field and option IDs are rendered into the `project-board` skill from `src/n3rv/board.py` — do not retype them.

